<%- include('../header.ejs') %>
<%- include('../nav.ejs') %>

<div class="col-12">
  <h1>Weekly fixtures post</h1>
  <p class="text-muted">
    Exactly what the Sunday post will contain. Nothing on this page sends anything.
  </p>

  <div class="alert <%= facebookConfigured ? 'alert-success' : 'alert-danger' %>">
    <strong>Facebook:</strong>
    <%= facebookConfigured
      ? 'configured — the division cards go up as one album.'
      : 'NOT configured. Set META_TAMESIDE_PAGE_ID and META_TAMESIDE_PAGE_TOKEN on the service.' %>
  </div>

  <div class="alert <%= instagramConfigured ? 'alert-success' : 'alert-warning' %>">
    <strong>Instagram:</strong>
    <% if (instagramConfigured) { %>
      configured — the division cards go up as one carousel.
    <% } else { %>
      not configured (<code>META_IG_USER_ID</code> is unset), so this posts to Facebook only.
      That is a supported setup, not a fault.
    <% } %>
  </div>

  <div class="alert alert-info">
    <strong>This post is new, not a replacement.</strong> Make.com never posted fixtures on
    either league's account, so there is nothing to disable and no double-post risk on the
    cutover — unlike the weekly tables post.
  </div>

  <% if (!fixtureCount) { %>
    <div class="alert alert-secondary">
      <strong>Nothing to post.</strong> There are no fixtures in the coming seven days, so
      the scheduled run would skip and send nothing. That is the normal state through the
      summer and over Christmas — an empty card reading "Fixtures this week" is worse than
      no post at all.
    </div>
  <% } else { %>
    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Images</h2>
    <p class="text-muted">
      <%= fixtureCount %> <%= fixtureCount === 1 ? 'match' : 'matches' %> across
      <%= divisions.length %> <%= divisions.length === 1 ? 'division' : 'divisions' %>.
      Rendered on demand as JPEG. <strong>Meta fetches these URLs itself, later, from its
      own servers</strong> — so they have to be public, and they have to still work minutes
      after the post is made. A division with no fixtures this week is left out rather than
      posted blank.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted small">
      The pictures below are served by <em>this</em> server, so what you are looking at is
      what this build renders. The link under each one is the absolute URL Meta will fetch.
    </p>
    <div class="row">
      <% imagePaths.forEach(function (src, i) { %>
        <div class="col-12 col-md-6 mb-3">
          <img src="<%= src %>" class="img-fluid border" alt="Fixtures card">
          <p class="small text-break mt-1"><a href="<%= images[i] %>"><%= images[i] %></a></p>
        </div>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  <% } %>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Captions</h2>
  <div class="row">
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 mb-3">
      <h3 class="h6">Facebook</h3>
      <pre class="border p-2 bg-light"><%= captions.facebook %></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 mb-3">
      <h3 class="h6">Instagram</h3>
      <pre class="border p-2 bg-light"><%= captions.instagram %></pre>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="text-muted">
    <% if (captions.mentioned.length) { %>
      Clubs mentioned on Instagram: <%= captions.mentioned.join(', ') %>. Only the clubs
      actually playing this week are named — a mention is a notification, and notifying a
      club about a week it is not playing in is how an account gets muted.
    <% } else { %>
      <strong>No clubs are mentioned</strong>, because no club has an Instagram handle
      stored against it. Add them on the club admin pages and the clubs playing each week
      appear here automatically. Facebook page mentions are omitted on purpose: they need
      the Pages API, and plain <code>@Club Name</code> text does nothing at all.
    <% } %>
  </p>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Send it</h2>
  <p class="text-muted">
    A dry run creates unpublished Instagram containers to ask Meta whether it would accept
    each image, then abandons them. Nothing becomes visible, and they expire in 24 hours.
    It proves Meta can <em>fetch</em> these URLs — which is the fault that actually recurs
    — not that the pictures read well. Look at them above for that.
  </p>
  <form method="post" action="/admin/social/weekly-fixtures?dry=1" class="d-inline">
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-secondary">Dry run (posts nothing)</button>
  </form>
  <form method="post" action="/admin/social/weekly-fixtures" class="d-inline ms-2"
        onsubmit="return confirm('This posts publicly to Facebook and Instagram now. Continue?');">
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-danger" <%= fixtureCount ? '' : 'disabled' %>>Post now</button>
  </form>
</div>

<%- include('../footer.ejs') %>
